{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q003_actin_like_atpase_divergence","answer":"SCOPe 2.08 places these catalytic domains in different families within the same Actin-like ATPase domain superfamily, c.55.1 (SUNID 53067): Actin/HSP70 is c.55.1.1 (53068), hexokinase is c.55.1.3 (53083), and glycerol kinase is c.55.1.4 (53089). Actin and the HSP70 ATPase portion therefore share a family; their relationship to the two kinase families is at superfamily level. All fall within the Ribonuclease H-like motif fold, c.55, in the alpha/beta class, c.

The shared superfamily supports probable common ancestry of their catalytic cores despite substantial functional divergence. This is stronger than sharing a fold or class, which alone would not establish homology. SCOPe also annotates the superfamily as a duplication containing two domains of this fold, so the relationship concerns the classified modules rather than equivalence of entire proteins.

Biologically, this is consistent with an ancestral nucleotide-handling architecture diversifying into actin’s cytoskeletal ATPase activity, HSP70’s chaperone-associated ATPase activity, and ATP-dependent phosphorylation of hexoses or glycerol. It does not permit transferring actin polymerization, HSP70 peptide binding or chaperone function, hexose specificity, or glycerol specificity between them. Nor does it establish identical catalytic mechanisms, regulation, or interchangeable modeling templates. Such transfers require sequence and active-site comparisons, structural alignments and ligand-bound structures, domain-context analysis, and biochemical evidence; a detailed evolutionary history additionally needs phylogenetic evidence. Those independent analyses were not retrieved here.","evidence_used":["scop-homology/SKILL.md","scop-homology/references/biological-interpretation.md","scop-homology/references/api-usage.md","Pretrained biological knowledge for functional context","mcp__scope__get_scop_service_info","mcp__scope__search_scop","mcp__scope__get_scop_node","mcp__scope__get_scop_domains","mcp__scope__list_scop_children","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=Actin&mode=auto&limit=8","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=Hexokinase&mode=auto&limit=5","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=Glycerol+kinase&mode=auto&limit=5","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1rgia1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1rgia1/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53068","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53068/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53068/children?limit=10","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53083","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53083/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53089","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53089/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53067","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53067/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53067/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53067/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53066/homology"]}]}
